Big fan of the latest release. Can I make a suggestion on the revalidate property. Since it's modeled after a cache header, why not make the functionality match that of a cache header? 

Google tends to be the first request for low traffic pages, so with this property they're likely crawling an outdated version of the page. There are times where a developer wants to get the latest version of a page even if it has to be regenerated. You could change the properties to `maxAge` and `staleWhileRevalidate`. It would give more control to the developer and as an added plus those familiar with cache headers would be familiar with this setting from the start and those who aren't would start to get familiar with web caching.

Either way it gives more control to the developer.

So instead of:

```javascript
// pages/blog/[slug].js
export async function getStaticProps({ params }) {
  const post = await getBlogPostBySlug(params.slug);
  return {
    // Set the timeout for generating to 1 second
    // This timeout could be longer depending on how often data changes
    revalidate: 1,
    props: {
      post,
    },
  };
}
```

Consider this:
```javascript
// pages/blog/[slug].js
export async function getStaticProps({ params }) {
  const post = await getBlogPostBySlug(params.slug);
  return {
    // Set the timeout for generating to 1 second
    // This timeout could be longer depending on how often data changes
    maxAge: 1,
    staleWhileRevalidate: 86400,
    props: {
      post,
    },
  };
}
```

Cheers! Keep pushing the web forward!

